section: compiler
synopsis: Add ``-Wspec-constr-reboxing``
description:
  New opt-in warning ``-Wspec-constr-reboxing``, which reports when the
  SpecConstr optimisation specialises a function on a constructor-shaped
  argument that the function also uses boxed, so that the specialised code
  re-allocates the constructor ("reboxing"). Reboxing can increase
  allocation and defeat sharing schemes based on pointer equality.
issues: #27628
mrs: !7
